WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.230
In a laboratory, volunteers put on a helmet
that sent weak magnetic fields across

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.980
the temporal lobes.

3
00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.230
Many of them reported a sensed presence.

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.870
In 2005, a double-blind repeat of the
test found no effect from the fields.

5
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.690
Yet people in every age and
culture report experiences of God.

6
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.100
If someone tells you they met
God, should you believe them?

7
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.450
And should they believe themselves?

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.840
In this mission, you'll meet Richard Swinburne's
principles of credulity and testimony.

9
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.640
Then you'll weigh the
challenges, from brain science,

10
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:38.120
from philosophy, and
from conflicting claims.

11
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: weigh up whether a claim
to have met God should be believed.
